"subscribers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/proteneer/timemachine/subscribers","subscription_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/proteneer/timemachine/subscription","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/proteneer/timemachine/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/proteneer/timemachine/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/proteneer/timemachine/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/proteneer/timemachine/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/proteneer/timemachine/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/proteneer/timemachine/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/proteneer/timemachine/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/proteneer/timemachine/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/proteneer/timemachine/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/proteneer/timemachine/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/proteneer/timemachine/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/proteneer/timemachine/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/proteneer/timemachine/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/proteneer/timemachine/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/proteneer/timemachine/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/proteneer/timemachine/deployments","created_at":"2018-12-26T14:25:45Z","updated_at":"2026-03-05T08:51:09Z","pushed_at":"2026-01-09T00:05:01Z","git_url":"git://github.com/proteneer/timemachine.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:proteneer/timemachine.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/proteneer/timemachine.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/proteneer/timemachine","homepage":"","size":20108,"stargazers_count":167,"watchers_count":167,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":19,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":25,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["forcefield-parameterization","free-energy-calculations","molecular-dynamics"],"visibility":"public","forks":19,"open_issues":25,"watchers":167,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"I'm in the middle of porting over a significant portion of the code to autograd/jax after discovering several bugs and annoyances in tensorflow:\r\n\r\n1) In tensorflow, the derivative of the norm of zero-length vector is NaN. This comes up all the time on the diagonals of things like pairwise distance matrices and is quite a nuisance to deal with.\r\n\r\n2) Tensorflow computes jacfwd by using the Pearlmutter trick of composing and transposing vJps. This is far less ideal because it still uses jacrevs. For functions such as forces, which map from ```F: R^N -> R^N ``` there is no advantage to jacrevs. Furthemore, a jacfwd first framework would allow us to move away from having to store intermediate 0th order terms. This is a huge advantage for differentiating through dynamics.\r\n\r\n3) Tensorflow's support of derivatives of functions ```F: R -> R``` that go through intermediate non-holomorphic complex-valued functions is just straight up **incorrect**. I've filed an issue here: https://github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow/issues/27845 but so far have not heard back. This is extremely important for when we want to start porting things like Ewald summations and periodic spaces.\r\n\r\n4) Through some clever tracing techniques, autograd/jax has an API that is isomorphic to numpy. This would allow us to rapidly port over existing code that already uses numpy with ease. There are some key differences though (things like in-place modifications) that we need to be care of. But nevertheless, it looks to be easier than porting to tensorflow or torch.\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/proteneer/timemachine/issues/73/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/proteneer/timemachine/issues/73/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tensorflow/tensorflow/issues/comments/485041842","html_url":"https://github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow/issues/27845#issuecomment-485041842","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tensorflow/tensorflow/issues/27845","id":485041842,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ4NTA0MTg0Mg==","user":{"login":"ymodak","id":42785357,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyNzg1MzU3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42785357?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ymodak","html_url":"https://github.com/ymodak","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ymodak/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ymodak/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ymodak/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ymodak/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ymodak/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ymodak/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ymodak/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ymodak/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ymodak/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-04-20T00:09:11Z","updated_at":"2019-04-20T00:09:11Z","body":"Thanks for the minimal code snippe